        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "It appears that the `*` here does not match files beginning with a dot:\n\nhttps://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/0ffc2af38b3c5293076317b138635d6d7c80a40f/lua/mini/sessions.lua#L489\n\nPerhaps doing two globs, one for `*` and one for `.*`? This seems to fix the issue.\n```lua\n  local globs = vim.fn.globpath(global_dir, '*') .. '\\n' .. vim.fn.globpath(global_dir, '.*')\n```\n\nWhile reading about `vim.fn.globpath`, I also noticed an option to have it return a list of paths instead, which has the advantage of handling filenames with a newline in them (probably not important here):\n```lua\n  -- local globs = vim.fn.globpath(global_dir, '*') .. '\\n' .. vim.fn.globpath(global_dir, '.*')\n  local globs =\n    vim.list_extend(vim.fn.globpath(global_dir, '*', false, true), vim.fn.globpath(global_dir, '.*', false, true))\n  if #globs == 0 then return {} end\n\n  local res = {}\n  -- for _, f in pairs(vim.split(globs, '\\n')) do\n  for _, f in pairs(globs) do\n    if H.is_readable_file(f) then\n      local s = H.new_session(f, 'global')\n      res[s.name] = s\n    end\n  end\n```\n\nI can submit a PR tomorrow if you'd like after adding an appropriate test case.",
